---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import PhoneCTA from '../../components/PhoneCTA.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import SchemaMarkup from '../../components/SchemaMarkup.astro';
import { config } from '../../config';

const title = 'Nanaimo to Victoria Courier';
const description = 'Same-day courier from Nanaimo to Victoria. Ferry or highway routing. 3–4 hour delivery. Legal documents, medical samples, rush parcels.';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <SchemaMarkup type="Service" data={{ serviceName: 'Nanaimo to Victoria Courier Route', description }} />

  <PageHero
    word="Victoria"
    eyebrow="Nanaimo → Victoria"
    description="Same-day delivery from Nanaimo to Victoria, with ferry routing optimized for schedule and time sensitivity — legal documents, medical specimens, rush parcels."
  />

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Nanaimo ↔ Victoria: Route Details</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-4 text-brand-blue">Ferry Route (Most Common)</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm">
          <li><strong>Distance:</strong> ~60 km via Departure Bay to Swartz Bay</li>
          <li><strong>Ferry time:</strong> 90 minutes sailing + 30 min wait/load</li>
          <li><strong>Drive time:</strong> 45 min Nanaimo to ferry + 30 min Swartz to Victoria</li>
          <li><strong>Total typical:</strong> 3–4 hours door-to-door</li>
          <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Ferry surcharge ~$25 added to base rate</li>
          <li><strong>Frequency:</strong> Ferries every 1–2 hours, peak schedules checked automatically</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-4 text-brand-blue">Highway Route (Alternate)</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm">
          <li><strong>Distance:</strong> ~260 km via Highway 1 (Malahat), Highway 19</li>
          <li><strong>Drive time:</strong> 3–3.5 hours one-way (Vancouver traffic if metro area)</li>
          <li><strong>Total typical:</strong> 4–5 hours (but avoids ferry wait)</li>
          <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Higher mileage charge, no ferry surcharge</li>
          <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Non-urgent, predictable timing (no ferry variability)</li>
          <li><strong>Note:</strong> Malahat can close in winter—ferry is safer in bad weather</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Same-Day Cutoff Times: Nanaimo to Victoria</h2>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Order your courier before these times for guaranteed same-day delivery:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Monday–Thursday</h3>
        <p class="text-lg text-brand-blue font-semibold">10:00 AM cutoff</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-1">Ferry routing recommended. Pickup by 10 AM gets your delivery to Victoria by 2–3 PM.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Friday</h3>
        <p class="text-lg text-brand-blue font-semibold">9:00 AM cutoff</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mt-1">Earlier cutoff due to afternoon ferry congestion. Plan ahead for Friday Victoria deliveries.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">After 10 AM?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Call us. We may still get it to Victoria same-day if ferry schedules align or highway routing works. Not guaranteed, but we'll try.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Common Nanaimo ↔ Victoria Scenarios</h2>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Law Firm Document Filing (Victoria Courts)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Order by 9 AM from Nanaimo law firm. We pick up, ferry to Victoria, file at courts by 1 PM. Proof of filing back to you by 3 PM.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Medical Specimen Transport</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Nanaimo clinic takes blood draw at 9 AM. We pick up, maintain temperature control during ferry, deliver to Victoria lab by noon. Results by end of business day.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-brand-blue bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Manufacturing Parts Delivery</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Nanaimo warehouse completes order by 10 AM. Same-day delivery to Victoria customer by 2 PM. Goods arrive in good condition, ready for production next day.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Ferry Timing Impact on Delivery (Critical in Winter)</h2>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Ferry schedules drive timing. Summer ferries run every 1–2 hours; winter may be less frequent. Key considerations:
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Spring–Fall (May–Oct)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Ferries: every 1–2 hours. Pickup by 10 AM, ferry departs 10:30–11 AM, arrives Victoria 12:30–1 PM, delivery by 2–3 PM. Reliable timing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Winter (Nov–Mar)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Ferries: every 2–3 hours. Order earlier (by 9 AM instead of 10 AM) to catch morning ferry. Afternoon orders risk next-day. Malahat highway closes occasionally; ferry becomes only option.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded border-l-4 border-brand-blue">
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Holiday/Peak Season (Summer Weekends)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">
          Ferry congestion. Order EARLY (by 9 AM) to secure spot. We prioritize early orders. Late orders may miss ferry and delay to next sailing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-50 section-container">
    <h2>Nanaimo ↔ Victoria Pricing & Cost Examples</h2>

    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
        Ferry-route pricing includes ferry surcharge. Highway routing available as backup if ferry is delayed or non-viable.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded border border-gray-300 mb-6 space-y-4">
        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Ferry Route (Standard Documents)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$35 base + (60 km × $2.00) + $25 ferry = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$145–$160</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Standard documents, letters, contracts. Example: Legal filing, business documents, medical records.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Ferry Route + Temperature Control (Medical)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$145 + $10 (refrigerated) = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$155–$170</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Lab specimens, pharmacy delivery. Temperature maintained during ferry crossing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Ferry Route + Oversized (Van)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$50 base + (60 km × $2.50) + $25 ferry = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$220–$240</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Equipment, parts, oversized goods. Requires larger vehicle; ferry accommodates.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pb-4 border-b">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Highway Route (Backup/Urgent)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">$45 base + (260 km × $2.50) = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$700–$750</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Bypass ferry via Malahat. Longer drive but avoids ferry scheduling. Use if ferry is delayed or not viable.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Rush Surcharge (After 10 AM)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700">Ferry route × 1.5 = <span class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-blue">~$215–$240</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-1">Emergency order after 10 AM cutoff. Still same-day if ferry space available. Malahat option triggered if ferry is full.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6">
        High-volume Nanaimo–Victoria account? Weekly or monthly ferry runs available at flat rates (~$120–$180/run, 30–50% savings). Law firms and medical offices often contract monthly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteForm />

  <section class="section-container">
    <h2>Nanaimo ↔ Victoria FAQ</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Does the ferry delay push my delivery to next day?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Not usually. We monitor ferry schedules and may switch to highway routing if ferry is significantly delayed. We'll update you if timeline changes. Always order by 10 AM to stay same-day.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">What if the Malahat closes (snow/weather)?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Ferry route is safer in winter. We'll re-route to ferry if highway is closed. Ferry surcharge applies, but your shipment still gets to Victoria same-day when possible.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Can I request the ferry route specifically?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Tell us "ferry preferred" and we'll route that way. Best for time-sensitive or weather-dependent shipments. Highway is cost-effective but less predictable in winter.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Do you track in real time across the ferry?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. You'll see the driver progress to Departure Bay, then pick up again after ferry crossing at Swartz Bay. Full delivery tracking to Victoria destination.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Can you handle a return pickup from Victoria?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Yes. Tell us if you need pickup in Victoria too (e.g., pick up files, deliver to Nanaimo). We'll dispatch accordingly and quote a round-trip.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
